---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { brand } from '../config/brand';
---
<Layout
  title="Our 5-Year Workmanship Warranty | Belvedere Decks"
  description="Every Belvedere Decks project carries a 5-year written workmanship warranty on top of the 25 to 50 year manufacturer board warranties. Here's exactly what it covers and how it works."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">The warranty</p>
      <h1>Five years on our work. In writing.</h1>
      <div class="rule"></div>
      <p class="lead">
        Two warranties protect every deck we build: the manufacturer's warranty on the
        boards, and ours on the workmanship. Here is what each one covers, with the
        conditions stated up front instead of discovered later.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>The 5-year workmanship warranty</h2>
      <p>
        We warrant our workmanship for five years from substantial completion of your
        project. If something we built fails because of how we built it, a board that
        was fastened wrong, trim that comes loose, a railing connection that loosens
        under normal use, we come back and correct it at no cost to you. That promise
        is written into your contract, not implied on a website.
      </p>

      <h2>The conditions, stated plainly</h2>
      <p>
        The warranty applies to the original homeowner at the project address and is
        non-transferable. It asks one thing of you: maintain the deck per the
        manufacturer's published care guidelines, which for composite amounts to soap,
        water, and common sense. It does not cover damage from misuse or neglect,
        alteration or repair by someone other than us, structural modification, or acts
        of nature. If a covered problem appears, call or email, we come look, and if our
        workmanship caused it, we fix it. No claim forms.
      </p>

      <h2>The manufacturer warranties, registered for you</h2>
      <p>
        TimberTech and Trex boards carry manufacturer warranties of 25 to 50 years
        depending on the line, covering material defects, fading, and staining. Most
        homeowners never see those warranties because nobody registers them. We register
        eligible product warranties on your behalf and hand you the documentation at
        completion, so the coverage actually exists when you need it.
      </p>

      <h2>Why five years and not a bigger number</h2>
      <p>
        Workmanship problems show up early: a bad fastener or a missed flashing detail
        announces itself within the first few seasons, not in year twelve. Five years
        covers that window with room to spare, and it is a number we can stand behind
        for every single project rather than an impressive one we would have to argue
        about later. The structure itself is protected differently: by building it to
        code, having the county inspect it, and using boards whose makers back them for
        decades.
      </p>

      <p>
        Questions about coverage on your project?
        <a href={`mailto:${brand.email}`}> {brand.email}</a>, or ask at the estimate
        visit and we will point to the exact contract language.
      </p>
      <p><a class="btn primary" href="/estimate">Get a Free Estimate</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
